Document (dev.stxt.website): PDF and Press | STXT

	Metadata:
		Last modif: 2026-11-15
		Description: stxt-pdf, the layout and PDF engine for STXT documents in Java, and stxt-press, the service that generates PDF and SVG on it, with templates filled with JSON data.

	Header: PDF and Press

	Assert >>
		[stxt-pdf](https://github.com/stxt-lang/stxt-pdf) converts an @STXT@ document into an
		accessible PDF. [stxt-press](https://github.com/stxt-lang/stxt-press) offers it as an
		HTTP service, with a web editor and a command line, and fills templates with JSON
		data.

	Code >>
		Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
			Language: en
			Title: Quarterly report
			Page:
				Paper: A4
				Margin: 50
			Styles:
				For element: Document
					Typography:
						Font: IBM Plex Sans
						Size: 10
			Section:
				Heading 1:
					Text: Quarterly report
				Paragraph: Sales grew by 12% compared with the previous quarter.

	Content >>
		The namespace `dev.stxt.pdf` describes the document:

		* **`Page`**: the paper and the margins.
		* **`Styles`**: the appearance, with rules by element, by style or by identifier.
		* **`Section`**: the content, with headings, paragraphs, tables, images, lists...

		The engine works out where everything goes, splits the content into pages and writes
		the PDF. Both projects read the @STXT@ with the [Java library](tools-java) and are not
		implementations of the language: syntax and schema errors carry the codes of the
		library (`NODE_NOT_DEFINED_IN_SCHEMA`...), and those of the engine, its own.

	Subheader: The PDF

	Content >>
		* **Embedded fonts**, with the characters that are used.
		* **Tagging** for accessibility: PDF/UA-1, or PDF/UA-2 on request.
		* **PDF/A** (2 and 3, `b` and `a`) on request, with embedded files for Factur-X.
		* **Bookmarks**, one for each heading.
		* **SVG**: besides the PDF, one image per page.

		**The engine is strict.** Each element only accepts the properties that make sense in
		it, and none has an appearance of its own: a `Heading 1` is not larger than a
		`Paragraph` unless a style says so. What would have no effect, contradicts itself or
		does not fit is an error with its line.

	Subheader: stxt-pdf

	Content >>
		The engine, as a Java library. It is published on Maven Central as
		[`dev.stxt:stxt-pdf`](https://central.sonatype.com/artifact/dev.stxt/stxt-pdf).

	Subsubheader: Installation

	Content >>
		Java 17 or later. The current version is 0.18.1.

	Xml >>
		<dependency>
		    <groupId>dev.stxt</groupId>
		    <artifactId>stxt-pdf</artifactId>
		    <version>0.18.1</version>
		</dependency>

	Content >>
		Or with Gradle:

	Listing >>
		implementation 'dev.stxt:stxt-pdf:0.18.1'

	Subsubheader: Converting a document

	Java >>
		import java.io.OutputStream;
		import java.nio.file.Files;
		import java.nio.file.Path;

		import dev.stxt.InlineNode;
		import dev.stxt.pdf.convert.Converter;
		import dev.stxt.pdf.stxt.DocumentReader;

		InlineNode doc = new DocumentReader().read(Path.of("report.stxt"));
		try (OutputStream out = Files.newOutputStream(Path.of("report.pdf"))) {
		    Converter.create().toPdf(doc, out);
		}

	Content >>
		`DocumentReader` reads and validates the document. `Converter` lays it out and writes
		the PDF. A `Converter` is created once and can be used from several threads at once.

	Subsubheader: Options

	Java >>
		Converter converter = Converter.builder()
		        .resources(new Resources(Path.of("my-resources")))   // another resources folder
		        .styles(Path.of("styles.stxt"))                       // a separate styles file
		        .pdfA(PdfA.A3B)                                       // PDF/A-3b
		        .build();

	Content >>
		| Option         | Default                                                                              |
		|----------------|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
		| `resources`    | The folder `resources/` of the working directory                                     |
		| `styles`       | None. Each call adds a styles file, and the last one wins                            |
		| `limits`       | 2000 pages, 25 million pixels per image and 20 MB per PDF, among others              |
		| `debug`        | `false`. With `true`, it paints the outline of each box                              |
		| `pdfUa`        | `1`: PDF/UA-1. With `2`, PDF/UA-2, in PDF 2.0                                        |
		| `pdfA`         | None. `PdfA.A2B`, `A2A`, `A3B` or `A3A`                                              |
		| `exclude`      | None. The checks that are no longer an error, such as `Check.CONTRAST`               |
		| `cancellation` | None. When to stop every conversion, for example after a time limit                  |

	Subsubheader: Resources

	Content >>
		The fonts and the images of a document are in a resources folder:

	Listing >>
		resources/
		    fonts/      .ttf and .otf fonts
		    images/     .png, .jpg and .svg images

	Content >>
		* Only the fonts of `fonts/` are used, never those of the system. Each file is
		  recognized by the family, the weight and the style it declares inside.
		* A variant that has no file (a weight the family does not have) is an error: the
		  closest one is not used.
		* `Image: logos/acme.png` is `resources/images/logos/acme.png`. Absolute paths, `..`
		  and links that leave the folder are not accepted.
		* The repository includes IBM Plex Sans, Serif and Mono, under the SIL Open Font
		  License.

	Subsubheader: Errors

	Content >>
		Every error is a `StxtPdfException` with its kind (`kind()`), its code (`code()`) and
		its line (`line()`, 0 if it is not of a line):

		| `kind()`           | What it is                                                               |
		|--------------------|--------------------------------------------------------------------------|
		| `INVALID_DOCUMENT` | An error of the document: syntax, schema or rules of the engine          |
		| `LIMIT`            | The document exceeds a limit: pages, pixels of an image, size            |
		| `CANCELLED`        | The conversion was stopped by its `cancellation`                         |
		| `RESOURCE`         | The configuration of the caller: the resources folder, a file            |
		| `INTERNAL`         | An error of the engine                                                   |

	Subsubheader: Documentation

	Content >>
		Everything is in the repository, in English and in Spanish:

		* [Manual](https://github.com/stxt-lang/stxt-pdf/blob/master/docs/en/manual/README.md):
		  how a document is written, from the first one to each element.
		* [Reference](https://github.com/stxt-lang/stxt-pdf/blob/master/docs/en/reference/README.md):
		  the exact rule of each behavior and the design decisions.
		* [Examples](https://github.com/stxt-lang/stxt-pdf/blob/master/test/examples/README.md):
		  real documents (invoice, letter, contract, annual report...) with their PDF.

	Subheader: stxt-press

	Content >>
		The service, in a single jar: an HTTP API, a web editor and a command line. The
		layout is that of stxt-pdf, and the fill of the Slots, that of
		[stxt-transform](https://github.com/stxt-lang/stxt-java-transform). The current
		version is 0.6.1.

	Subsubheader: Starting

	Content >>
		With Docker, the image
		[`ghcr.io/stxt-lang/stxt-press`](https://github.com/stxt-lang/stxt-press/pkgs/container/stxt-press),
		for `linux/amd64` and `linux/arm64`:

	Listing >>
		docker run --rm -p 127.0.0.1:8080:8080 ghcr.io/stxt-lang/stxt-press:0.6.1

	Content >>
		The index and the editor are at `http://127.0.0.1:8080/`, with example templates and
		documents. The image answers without token to anyone who reaches its port:
		`127.0.0.1` keeps it on the machine.

		Own templates, documents or resources replace those of the image:

	Listing >>
		docker run --rm -p 127.0.0.1:8080:8080 \
		    -v "$PWD/templates:/opt/stxt-press/templates:ro" \
		    -v "$PWD/documents:/opt/stxt-press/documents:ro" \
		    -v "$PWD/resources:/opt/stxt-press/resources:ro" \
		    ghcr.io/stxt-lang/stxt-press:0.6.1

	Content >>
		Without Docker, the folder
		[`server/`](https://github.com/stxt-lang/stxt-press/tree/master/server) of the
		repository is a whole server (the jar, its configuration, the fonts and the
		examples). It needs Java 17 or later:

	Listing >>
		server/start.sh

	Subsubheader: Templates and Slots

	Content >>
		A template is a `dev.stxt.pdf` document with **Slots**, the places that wait for a
		piece of data:

	Code >>
		Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
			Language: en
			Title: Invoice ${number}
			Page:
				Paper: A4
				Margin: 50
			Styles:
				For element: Document
					Typography:
						Font: IBM Plex Sans
						Size: 10
			Section:
				Heading 1:
					Text: Invoice ${number}
				Paragraph: Customer: ${customer}
				Paragraph: [lines]${item}: ${amount} €

	Content >>
		With these data:

	Json >>
		{
		    "number": "2026-0142",
		    "customer": "Athena Bookshop",
		    "lines": [
		        { "item": "A5 notebooks", "amount": "120.00" },
		        { "item": "HB pencils", "amount": "36.00" }
		    ]
		}

	Content >>
		The filled document, the one that is laid out, ends like this:

	Listing >>
		Section:
			Heading 1:
				Text: Invoice 2026-0142
			Paragraph: Customer: Athena Bookshop
			Paragraph: A5 notebooks: 120.00 €
			Paragraph: HB pencils: 36.00 €

	Content >>
		| Slot                                         | What it does                                                                |
		|----------------------------------------------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|
		| `<var>`                                      | Puts a value, and ends the value of the node                                |
		| `{object}`                                   | Enters an object                                                            |
		| `[list]`                                     | Repeats the node once for every element                                     |
		| `${var}`                                     | Puts a value inside text, looking it up from the element up to the root     |
		| `<?var>`, `{?object}`, `[?list]`, `${?var}`  | Optional: with no data, the node is removed (or the text gets nothing)      |
		| `$${`                                        | A literal `${`                                                              |

		A required Slot with no data is an error (`SLOT_NO_DATA`). The Slots follow
		[@STXT@ Transform](stxt-transform-ref), which is in `Genesis`: they may change with it.

	Subsubheader: Templates and documents of the server

	Content >>
		The server prints two kinds of files, each from its own folder:

		* **A template** (`/print`): it is filled with the JSON data of the request, or with
		  its sample data.
		* **A document** (`/documents`): it is printed as it is, without data.

	Listing >>
		templates/
		    .styles.stxt                the styles of every template
		    invoices/
		        .styles.stxt            the styles of the templates of invoices/
		        invoice.stxt            the template invoices/invoice
		        invoice.styles.stxt     its own styles
		        invoice.json            its sample data

	Content >>
		A template is named by its path without extension (`invoices/invoice`). The styles
		apply from the root to the template, and the nearest one wins. Documents follow the
		same rules, without data. The folders are read on every request: a file changed on
		disk counts without restarting.

	Subsubheader: Routes

	Content >>
		| Route                    | What it does                                                                                     |
		|--------------------------|--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
		| `GET /print/{path}`      | The template, filled with its sample data                                                        |
		| `POST /print/{path}`     | The template, filled with the body: the JSON data as they are                                    |
		| `GET /documents/{path}`  | The document, as it is                                                                           |
		| `POST /render`           | Any document: `{"document": "...", "styles": ["..."], "data": {...}, "options": {...}}`          |
		| `GET /schema`            | The schema `dev.stxt.pdf` of the engine                                                          |
		| `GET /health`            | The status and the versions, without token                                                       |

		`/print`, `/documents` and `/render` answer with a PDF (`?format=pdf`, the default),
		one SVG per page (`?format=svg`) or the filled document (`?format=stxt`).
		`&debug=true` paints the outlines of the boxes. The example invoice of the server,
		with its sample data and with those of a file:

	Listing >>
		curl -o invoice.pdf http://127.0.0.1:8080/print/examples/invoice
		curl -o invoice.pdf -d @data.json http://127.0.0.1:8080/print/examples/invoice

	Content >>
		An error is a JSON body with its code. Those of a conversion also carry their kind,
		their line and the input the line belongs to (`document`, `data`, `filled`, a styles
		file...):

	Json >>
		{"kind": "INVALID_DOCUMENT", "code": "JSON_NOT_VALID", "line": 2, "source": "data", "message": "..."}

	Subsubheader: Command line

	Content >>
		The commands of the jar have the names of the routes:

		| Command                              | What it does                                                                     |
		|--------------------------------------|----------------------------------------------------------------------------------|
		| `start`                              | Starts the HTTP service with its `server.stxt`                                   |
		| `render <document> -o <file>`        | Converts a document to PDF, with `--styles`, `--data`, `--pdf-ua`, `--pdf-a`...  |
		| `print <template> -o <file>`         | Converts a template of the templates folder                                      |
		| `documents <document> -o <file>`     | Converts a document of the documents folder                                      |
		| `fill <document> --data <file>`      | Writes the document with its Slots filled                                        |

		From the root of the repository, with the invoice above:

	Listing >>
		java -jar server/stxt-press.jar fill invoice.stxt --data invoice.json
		java -jar server/stxt-press.jar render invoice.stxt --data invoice.json -o invoice.pdf --config server/server.stxt

	Content >>
		An error is written to stderr with its file and its line:

	Listing >>
		stxt-press: invoice.stxt:15: SLOT_NO_DATA: Node 'Paragraph': No data for ${customer}

	Content >>
		The exit code is `0` if the job ends well, `1` if it fails (the document, its data, a
		resource, a limit) and `2` if the invocation is not valid. A file of `-o` is replaced
		only when the job ends well.

	Subsubheader: Configuration

	Content >>
		A server is configured with a `server.stxt` file, validated with the schema
		`dev.stxt.press` of the jar:

	Code >>
		Server (dev.stxt.press):
			Host: 0.0.0.0
			Port: 8080
			Token env: STXT_PRESS_TOKEN
			Resource folder: resources
			Template folder: templates
			Document folder: documents
			Routes:
				Render: false
				Save: true
			Limits:
				Timeout: 20
				Max pages: 500

	Content >>
		Without a file, the server listens on `127.0.0.1:8080`, without token and without
		templates or documents. Relative paths are relative to the folder of `server.stxt`.
		Every node is in the [README](https://github.com/stxt-lang/stxt-press#configuration).

	Subsubheader: Security

	Content >>
		The server has no TLS or users: it is meant to run behind a reverse proxy that adds
		them.

		* **Token**: with `Token env`, every route but `/health` and the pages asks for
		  `Authorization: Bearer <token>`.
		* **Local names**: without token and on a loopback address, it only answers requests
		  whose `Host` is local, against *DNS rebinding*.
		* **Routes off**: `Render: false`, `Files: false` and `Editor: false` in `Routes`
		  leave only the printing of the templates and the documents.

	Subheader: Versions

	Content >>
		Both projects are in 0.x. Until 1.0, the namespace `dev.stxt.pdf`, the Java API, the
		routes and `server.stxt` may change between minor versions, and so may the PDF of a
		valid document. Each change is in the `CHANGELOG.md` of its repository.
